<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-NatCon struggles with profits.</title>
<headline>RTRS-NatCon struggles with profits.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>18 months ended December 31</p>
<p>	    (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    21.59 vs 24.91</p>
<p>    Net					3.40 vs 18.98</p>
<p>    Abnormal items		 loss 18.08 vs loss 4.14</p>
<p>    Final dividend (cents)	     3.0  vs 3.0</p>
<p>NOTE: National Consolidated Ltd is an engineering group about 48.5 percent owned by Malaysia Mining Corp Bhcd. It has changed its financial year-end to December from June but said net profit after abnormals in the latest six months fell to A$6.2 million from A$7.4 million a year ago.  </p>
<p>    Total dividend (cents)		9.0 vs 6.0</p>
<p>    Sales				  543.57 vs 383.64</p>
<p>    Other income			  22.37 vs 10.81</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			   10.4  vs 11.9</p>
<p>Dividend is nil franked</p>
<p>Pay date May 23</p>
<p>Reg date May 9</p>
<p>    Tax					0.11 vs 1.8</p>
<p>    Interest				 9.30 vs 6.11</p>
<p>    Depreciation			  20.41 vs 14.09</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
